''This starts with Knargon Lanenda in the rogue guild.  He responds to several different questions about people and places. If you ask him about Jracol.. ''

: Knargon Lanenda says, 'I don't why [Carson] likes that guy ... he's certainly been nothing but trouble for me.' 

You say, 'Who is Carson?'

: Knargon Lanenda says 'Carson McCabe? He runs that sham of a fortress called [Highpass Hold]. We've been dealing with him for a few years, now. But, lately he seems to be losing control of his business. [Hanns] will whip him into shape pretty soon though, I bet.' 

''(This is a bit of foreshadowing to the follow-up quest to this).''

Ask him, "What is the shipment?"

: Knargon Lanenda says 'We have a small shipment of goods coming in later tonight. The [courier] will be waiting outside the city gates. Casually tell the courier [Lovely night for a stroll], and give him this old card as proof that you work for us. Make certain that you are not followed, and return the shipment to me.' 

Receive a Bent Playing Card. 

You say, 'What courier?' 

: Knargon Lanenda says 'The courier that usually runs [McCabe]'s shipment, is that good for nothing J'Racol. I don't trust his kind.' 

'''Back to the quest: Jracol Brestiage is the Dark Elf with Highpass faction who hangs outside the north gate in the North Qeynos zone. If you hang a right coming out of the north gate and follow the wall, you should see him standing by the wall or by a tree close to the zone. He is only around at night between 8 PM to 5 AM. '''

You say, 'Lovely night for a stroll.' 

: Jracol Brestiage says 'Yes, it is a lovely night for a walk, especially with a good friend. Tell me, are you a [friend]?'

You say, 'I am a friend.'  

: Jracol Brestiage says 'My memory is a bit fuzzy. If you are a friend, prove it to me.' 

'''Hand him the Bent Playing Card.'''

: Jracol Brestiage says 'Ah, good, it seems we have much in common after all. Take this back to the Circle, before the city guards come nosing around over here.'

